{"id":96,"name":"drowzee","speciesId":96,"dex":96,"form":"normal","generation":1,"types":["psychic"],"stats":{"hp":60,"attack":48,"defense":45,"special-attack":43,"special-defense":90,"speed":42},"abilities":[{"name":"insomnia","hidden":false},{"name":"forewarn","hidden":false},{"name":"inner-focus","hidden":true}],"height":10,"weight":324,"baseExp":66,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/96.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/96.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/96.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/96.ogg","genus":"Hypnosis Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"Puts enemies to sleep then eats their dreams. Occasionally gets sick from eating bad dreams."},{"version":"yellow","text":"If you sleep by it all the time, it will sometimes show you dreams it has eaten in the past."},{"version":"gold","text":"If you think that you had a good dream, but you can't remember it, a DROWZEE has probably eaten it."},{"version":"silver","text":"It remembers every dream it eats. It rarely eats the dreams of adults because children's are much tastier."},{"version":"crystal","text":"When it twitches its nose, it can tell where someone is sleeping and what that person is dreaming about."},{"version":"ruby","text":"If your nose becomes itchy while you are sleeping, it’s a sure sign that one of these POKéMON is standing above your pillow and trying to eat your dream through your nostrils."},{"version":"emerald","text":"If your nose becomes itchy while you are sleeping, it’s a sure sign that a DROWZEE is standing above your pillow and trying to eat your dream through your nostrils."},{"version":"firered","text":"A descendent of the legendary animal baku, which is said to eat dreams. It is skilled at hypnotism."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"Puts enemies to sleep, then eats their dreams. Occasionally gets sick from eating only bad dreams."},{"version":"diamond","text":"It can tell what people are dreaming by sniffing with its big nose. It loves fun dreams."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"If you think that you had a good dream but you can’t remember it, a DROWZEE has probably eaten it."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"It remembers every dream it eats. It rarely eats the dreams of adults because children’s are much tastier."},{"version":"y","text":"If you think that you had a good dream but you can’t remember it, a Drowzee has probably eaten it."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"If your nose becomes itchy while you are sleeping, it’s a sure sign that one of these Pokémon is standing above your pillow and trying to eat your dream through your nostrils."},{"version":"sun","text":"A Pokémon that nourishes itself by eating dreams, it is thought to share common ancestry with Munna and Musharna."},{"version":"moon","text":"It finds really fun dreams tasty. When it makes friends with people, it may show them the most delicious dreams it’s ever eaten."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"It can be spotted near recreational facilities, intending to eat the pleasant dreams of children who enjoyed themselves there that day."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"It puts its prey to sleep and devours their dreams. It seems that bad dreams taste sour, so Drowzee doesn’t particularly like eating them."},{"version":"lets-go-pikachu","text":"If you sleep by it all the time, it will sometimes show you dreams it had eaten in the past."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":190,"eggGroups":["humanshape"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"drowzee","speciesId":96,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 26"],"species":"hypno","speciesId":97,"evolvesTo":[]}]},"varieties":[{"id":96,"name":"drowzee","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/ot